=== STEP 7 — DERIVE STATE (the tracker has no 延遲; 完成 / 暫停 are read, not derived) ===
For every tracker row with Priority P0 or P1 (and any P2 that is OVERDUE):
- ENDS_SOON: 結束 is a real date within 14 days and 狀態 ∈ {進行中, 未開始}. Never flag a 完成 / 放棄 / 暫停 row.
- OVERDUE: 狀態 = 進行中 and 結束 < today; OR 狀態 = 未開始 and 開始 < today.
- DONE / PAUSED: 狀態 = 完成 → report as delivered and drop from load; 狀態 = 暫停 → report as paused AND cross-check the newest [3.1] block (a paused row that is visibly running is an SOR divergence worth block 01).
- UNDATED: 開始 or 結束 is blank / the literal `YYYY-MM-DD` (P0/P1 only). A P0 UNDATED counts as escalation-worthy (block 01) if the item has been in the tracker for >2 weeks — treat all P0 UNDATED as escalation-worthy in this first run and say so.
- UNDATED applies only to LIVE rows (進行中 / 未開始). A 完成, 放棄 or 暫停 row with placeholder dates is NOT a missing-dates ask.
- CHANGED: if PREV (STEP 5c) was readable, any of 狀態 / 開始 / 結束 / 負責人 that differs between PREV's row and today's tracker row (match by #; a row absent from PREV is new). Print each as `<field>: <old> → <new>`. No PREV → write `CHANGED not measured — no readable Ledger snapshot` once in block 08.
- PROPOSE_DONE: 狀態 = 進行中 but 備註 or the weekly log says shipped/上線/完成 → propose 完成. It belongs to the Friday approval cycle (zynkr-ops-weekly): if last week's Proposals carry that # → `in Friday's 【待核准】 list`; otherwise → `goes to Friday's propose`. Until that cycle writes the tracker itself (its Phase 3b, due by end of October), the owner still sets 完成 by hand after approval — say so. You never edit the tracker.
- DIRECTION_UNLABELLED: a P0 whose 備註 (and Refresh block, if read) carries neither 已定案 nor 還在摸索.
- STALLED: only against STALL (STEP 5c, a Ledger snapshot at least 14 days old). A P0/P1 row with 狀態 = 進行中 is STALLED when, versus STALL, none of 狀態/開始/結束/負責人 changed (備註 is not comparable on this read) AND the newest two weekly-log blocks do not mention it (its # or two words of its 項目) AND last week's Reports do not mention it. No readable STALL → write `STALLED not computable — no Ledger snapshot 14+ days old yet` (or `… not readable this run`) once in block 08; do not guess.
Also build a per-owner rollup: for each 負責人 → P0 ids · P1 ids · UNDATED ids · OVERDUE ids · ENDS_SOON ids · newest weekly-log block that mentions their function. GM load = share of P0 rows whose 負責人 is the GM.

=== STEP 8 — COMPOSE THE BRIEF (fixed order, English prose, every source linked) ===
Budgets, and they are enforced: each block-01 card ≤60 words and ≤5 lines; each block-02 bullet ≤20 words; each block-03 table cell ≤12 words; the whole email ≤900 words. One clause per bullet, one idea per sentence. If block 03 runs long it is carrying prose that belongs nowhere.
00 · Runway (always the first line) — computed in STEP 4b from the finance ledger (the KPI Dashboard's two Finance rows are a mirror; if they disagree with the ledger, the ledger wins and block 05 asks Peter to refresh them). If `constraints.burn_window` is unruled, the line carries BOTH runway figures and the state is the WORSE of the two. Format: `Runway <N> months · burn NT$<x>k / cap NT${{constraints.burn_cap_ntd_per_month}} · books as of <as-of>`, with the KPI Dashboard name linked. RED if N < {{constraints.runway_floor_months}}, or as-of older than {{constraints.books_stale_days}} days, or NO runway Actual exists (then write `RED · Runway is not being measured — no Actual in the KPI Dashboard`, and a second line naming who can fix it and by doing what). AMBER within 0.5 month of the floor. GREEN otherwise. If RED for a second week running, say `Second week running.`
01 · Decisions only you can make (≤3) — from: OPEN 待決事項 rows past/within 7 days of their 期限 or with no 期限 that block a P0; P0 rows owned by the GM with 結束 ≤14 days; P0 UNDATED; a Ledger 待決 from last Thursday that blocks a P0; APPROVAL = unconfirmed when a proposal in it touches a P0 (the close-it action is `reply to the 【待核准】 thread`, linked to that thread — approvals are the GM's alone). Three at most. THIS BLOCK IS THE WHOLE POINT OF THE BRIEF — if the reader finishes it still asking "so what do you want from me?", the brief has failed no matter how accurate the rest is. Write each one as a DECISION CARD in exactly this shape and order:
  `<N>. <the question, plain English, ending in "?">` / `Options — A: <option> · B: <option>` (or `Fill in — <what value> in <where>`) / `If you don't — <the concrete consequence, one clause>` / `Close it — <the one action> → <link>` / `Where this came from — <one clause> → <link>`
  D1 · ONE question per card. A row that bundles four decisions is four questions: ask the single one that unblocks the most and add `Same row also holds: <n> more — answer them in the same cell.` Never hand over four things joined by `·` and call it a decision — that is unanswerable, and it is the most common way this block fails.
  D2 · The question names the THING, not its code. ✅ `Which price list governs the enterprise AI diagnostic — the B2B pricing sheet, or a separate project rate?` ❌ `價格帶 vs [2.1] SOR · 保證條款 · pilot 楔子`.
  D3 · OPTIONS ARE MANDATORY. State the real alternatives (A/B/C), or the exact value and the exact place it goes (`Fill in — an end date in 結束 for rows 2.02, 6.03, 7.01`). If you cannot state the options, it is research, not a decision: drop it from 01 and put the research step in 03 or 06 instead.
  D4 · Open the source before writing the question. When a 待決事項 row's own text is shorthand, resolve it to the real choice. Restating the shorthand is not summarising — it just forwards the confusion. If the referenced document or section cannot be found, say exactly that and make fixing the pointer the ask.
  D5 · "Close it" is ONE action ending in a stamped artefact — a value typed in a named cell, a date on a tracker row, a message sent. Never "a conversation", never "align on". Name the tab, the row number and the column (`待決事項 row 1, 決議紀錄`) and link the file.
02 · Two clocks — Cash clock (from 00; at this burn the floor is reached on <date>; if runway is unmeasured write `Stopped — no figure to run.` and nothing else) · Calendar clock (days to Q3 end {{constraints.q3_end}} and H2 end {{constraints.h2_end}}; every P0/P1 with 結束 ≤30 days: id · item · owner · date; include the course tracker's next milestone End). One clause each — a milestone needing a paragraph belongs in 03.
03 · P0 / P1 status by LOB — one table per 主類別 in tracker order: # · Item · Owner · Status · Derived · Evidence (one clause naming where you saw it, linked) · Next. Every P0 exactly once. P2 only if OVERDUE. Cells ≤12 words — this is a scan surface, not a narrative. Where the tracker and another source disagree, say which wins under precedence and put the reconciliation in Next. If the Monday team recap (STEP 5c d — never the `沒有產出` notice) is in Sent, put one linked line above the tables — `Last week's change list went to the team: <subject>` — and do not restate its items. A PROPOSE_DONE row's Next is its place in the Friday cycle (STEP 7).
04 · Per-owner summary — one line per owner (named as the tracker names them): P0 · P1 · UNDATED · OVERDUE · ENDS_SOON · what the brief needs from them · when they were last heard from (their newest Ledger Reports post, else the newest weekly-log mention; for {{gm_name}}, also `this week: <OWNER LINE>` from STEP 5b). End with `GM holds <k>/<n> P0s (<pct>%)`.
05 · KPI off-target + missing numbers — (a) Off target: rows with BOTH a target and an Actual where the Actual misses the current quarter's target; (b) Missing: rows with no Actual → metric · owner · how it would be filled; CRM/accounting-backed ones marked `(not readable on a scheduled run)`. Batch by owner.
06 · Decisions register — table: id · Item · Label (`已定案` / `還在摸索` / unlabelled) · Decider · decide-by (or "no deadline") · Status · Source (linked). Sources: 待決事項 rows (all, open first); last week's Ledger Decisions rows (待決 first; Source `Thursday meeting <會議日期>`); an unconfirmed Friday approval (Source `【待核准】 <LAST WEEK>`, linked); DIRECTION_UNLABELLED P0s; the two known strategy-level open decisions if not already listed (course platform: build vs use an existing one, pending cohort ROAS; B2C high-ticket vs shifting to B2B) marked "no deadline" unless a date exists. The three promoted into 01 appear here too, marked `→ see 01`, so the register stays whole.
07 · Deliberately not this week — 3–5 named skips (e.g. P0s scheduled to start later — protect the date, don't half-start; items whose owner is out; P1/P2 with no date pressure) with one clause each.
08 · Machine health — the weekly-insights mail (its `laptop:` lines from STEP 5b, or that it did not arrive); livestream-curation last date (+ flag); SOR docs changed in the last 7 days (or "modifiedTime not exposed — skipped"); sources unavailable in this cloud run (CRM · calendar); tab-level deep links unavailable (Drive connector exposes no gid); DEAD REFERENCES — any `[N.N]` code or `§` section named by a source that resolves to no real document; the idempotency result; the Ledger line from STEP 5c (which beats recorded last week; tabs the snippet did not reach); CHANGED / STALLED availability from STEP 7.
One-line focus for the subject: the single most important thing from block 01, in plain English, ≤10 words, naming the thing at stake rather than its code. Good: `4 pricing decisions are 3 days overdue`. Bad: `§D 決策逾期 3 天`.
BEFORE YOU RENDER, run this check and rewrite anything that fails: (1) does every 01 card ask ONE question ending in a question mark? (2) could the reader answer it without opening another document? (3) does every card give real options, or the exact value and cell? (4) is every document, sheet and tab named anywhere in the brief a hyperlink? (5) is there a `[N.N]` code, `§` reference or acronym that is never expanded? (6) is any dead reference passed off as a citation instead of reported in 08? (7) read block 01 aloud — does it sound like a person telling you what they need?

