=== STEP 10 — DELIVER (exactly one message) ===
Subject: `{{routine.subject_prefix}}<YYYY-MM-DD> (W<ww>) — <one-line focus>`. Call the Gmail connector's send_message with to = {{recipients}} (plain emails, no display names), subject = the subject above, htmlBody = the Step-9 HTML, and body = a short plain-text alternative: the 00 runway line, then each 01 card as `<N>. <question>` / `A: … B: …` / `Close it — <action>: <raw URL>`. The plain-text part must still let the reader answer without opening the HTML, so keep the questions and options — never replace it with "see the HTML version". Send exactly ONE message; no cc/bcc. If send_message is unavailable or is refused, call create_draft with the same to/subject/htmlBody instead, and say in the report that delivery was a DRAFT, not a send. Never send more than one message; never also draft after a successful send.

=== STEP 11 — REPORT ===
Reply with: ISO week · delivered as SENT or DRAFT (+ message/draft id) · the 00 runway line · the block-01 list verbatim · counts (P0 OVERDUE / UNDATED / ENDS_SOON) · sources that could not be read · whether idempotency skipped the run. Never swallow an error silently.
